# Line-ending policy.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS: 60 tracked text files were once stored in git with
# DOUBLED line endings (\r\r\n), which MSVC reports as
#     warning C4335: Mac file format detected
# on every build. They are now stored with LF (issue #19); this file keeps
# it that way: git stores these types as LF and converts on checkout.
#
# If it ever recurs, do NOT reach for `git add --renormalize .` -- it cleans
# the WORKING-TREE file, strips only the CR directly before each LF, and so
# turns \r\r\n into \r\n in the repo (still CRLF), and a second run changes
# nothing. Strip every CR from the files themselves, then `git add`.

*                text=auto

# Explicit for the source we compile, so this survives someone narrowing the
# catch-all above.
*.cpp            text
*.h              text
*.md             text
*.txt            text
*.cmake          text
*.yml            text
*.py             text
*.dat            text

# Shell scripts must keep LF even on Windows checkouts -- a CR in a shebang
# line makes the interpreter path unrunnable.
*.sh             text eol=lf

# Windows batch files need CRLF; a lone LF can break `goto` and label parsing
# in cmd.exe.
*.bat            text eol=crlf

# Binary -- never touch these.
*.png            binary
*.jpg            binary
*.ico            binary
*.qm             binary
*.db             binary
